    "//@version=5\nindicator(\"x\")\nw = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, \"W\", ta.sma(close, 10))\nplot(w)": "<section class=\"_wrap_5ff86c\" aria-labelledby=\"uct-pine-head\" data-testid=\"pine-box\"><h3 class=\"_head_5ff86c\" id=\"uct-pine-head\">Paste a script or a formula</h3><p class=\"_hint_5ff86c\">A TradingView <b>Pine</b> indicator, a thinkorswim <b>thinkScript</b> study, a <b>TC2000</b> formula, or one of this engine's own. Everything the screen would read is listed below, in this engine's own words, before anything is saved.</p><textarea class=\"_area_5ff86c\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" rows=\"8\" placeholder=\"//@version=5\nindicator(&quot;My screen&quot;)\nr = ta.rsi(close, 14)\nplot(r < 30 and close > ta.sma(close, 200) ? 1 : 0, &quot;Signal&quot;)\" aria-label=\"Script or formula\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//@version=5\nindicator(\"x\")\nw = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, \"W\", ta.sma(close, 10))\nplot(w)</textarea><div class=\"_editor_18fb12\" data-testid=\"pine-editor\" data-dialect=\"pine\"><div class=\"cm-editor ͼ1 ͼ2 \"><div class=\"cm-announced\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"cm-scroller\"><div class=\"cm-gutters cm-gutters-before\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"min-height: 84px; position: sticky;\"><div class=\"cm-gutter cm-gutter-lint\"></div></div><div style=\"tab-size: 4;\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocorrect=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" writingsuggestions=\"false\" translate=\"no\" contenteditable=\"true\" class=\"cm-content cm-lineWrapping\" role=\"textbox\" aria-multiline=\"true\" aria-label=\"Script or formula editor\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"pine\"><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_comment_18fb12\">//@version=5</span></div><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_keyword_18fb12\">indicator</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"_string_18fb12\">\"x\"</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">)</span></div><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_name_18fb12\">w</span> <span class=\"_operator_18fb12\">=</span> <span class=\"_namespace_18fb12\">request</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">.</span><span class=\"_name_18fb12\">security</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"_namespace_18fb12\">syminfo</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">.</span><span class=\"_name_18fb12\">tickerid</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">,</span> <span class=\"_string_18fb12\">\"W\"</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">,</span> <span class=\"_namespace_18fb12\">ta</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">.</span><span class=\"_name_18fb12\">sma</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"_series_18fb12\">close</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">,</span> <span class=\"_number_18fb12\">10</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">))</span></div><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_keyword_18fb12\">plot</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"_name_18fb12\">w</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">)</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"_report_5ff86c\"><p class=\"_meta_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-meta\" data-dialect=\"pine\">Read as Pine script v5 · indicator() · “x”</p><p class=\"_meta_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"import-outcome\" data-outcome=\"disclosed\" role=\"status\"><b>Imported, with disclosed differences</b> — 1 difference can change a value or when it appears</p><fieldset class=\"_outputs_5ff86c\"><legend class=\"_legend_5ff86c\">This script offers one column</legend><label class=\"_outputRow_5ff86c\"><input type=\"radio\" checked=\"\" name=\"uct-pine-output\"><span class=\"_outKind_5ff86c\">plot</span><span class=\"_outTitle_5ff86c\">line 4</span><code class=\"_outFormula_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-formula-0\">tf(sma(close, 10), 'W')</code><span class=\"_outReadback_5ff86c\">(the 10-bar average of close) on the weekly timeframe</span></label></fieldset><ul class=\"_notes_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-vendor-notes\"><li class=\"_note_5ff86c\" data-vendor-note=\"htfLookaheadOffStepBacks\"><span class=\"_noteWhere_5ff86c\">Higher-timeframe timing differs from TradingView</span><span>This script reads a higher timeframe with request.security (lookahead off). UCT shows a weekly or monthly value only from the first bar AFTER that period has closed. TradingView shows it already on the bar that completes the period (for example, the week's close appears on Friday's daily bar) and, on a forming bar, shows the still-forming period. So on a daily chart this line is one bar later than TradingView on the last bar of every week (about 1 bar in 5) or month (about 1 in 21). UCT never shows a period's value before it has closed.</span></li></ul><div class=\"_notesWrap_5ff86c\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"_notesToggle_5ff86c\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-testid=\"pine-notes-toggle\">Show 1 line a screen does not read</button></div><p class=\"_refLink_5ff86c\"><a href=\"/formulas/reference\">See every name you can write →</a><a href=\"/formulas/library\">Browse what other members published →</a></p><div class=\"_toScreen_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-to-screen\"><span class=\"_toScreenLead_5ff86c\">This column is a number, so it can be charted as it is. To SCREEN with it, say what you are looking for:</span><div class=\"_toScreenRow_5ff86c\"><code class=\"_toScreenCol_5ff86c\">tf(sma(close, 10), 'W')</code><select class=\"_toScreenOp_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-screen-op\" aria-label=\"comparison\"><option value=\">\">is above</option><option value=\"<\">is below</option><option value=\">=\">is at or above</option><option value=\"<=\">is at or below</option><option value=\"==\">equals</option><option value=\"!=\">is not</option></select><input class=\"_toScreenValue_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-screen-value\" aria-label=\"threshold\" inputmode=\"decimal\" placeholder=\"value\" type=\"text\" value=\"\"></div><span class=\"_toScreenWhy_5ff86c\">Leave this blank to keep the column as it is — you can still chart it.</span></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"_useBtn_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-use\">Use this formula</button></div></section>",
    "//@version=5\nindicator(\"x\")\nplot(ta.cum(volume))": "<section class=\"_wrap_5ff86c\" aria-labelledby=\"uct-pine-head\" data-testid=\"pine-box\"><h3 class=\"_head_5ff86c\" id=\"uct-pine-head\">Paste a script or a formula</h3><p class=\"_hint_5ff86c\">A TradingView <b>Pine</b> indicator, a thinkorswim <b>thinkScript</b> study, a <b>TC2000</b> formula, or one of this engine's own. Everything the screen would read is listed below, in this engine's own words, before anything is saved.</p><textarea class=\"_area_5ff86c\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" rows=\"8\" placeholder=\"//@version=5\nindicator(&quot;My screen&quot;)\nr = ta.rsi(close, 14)\nplot(r < 30 and close > ta.sma(close, 200) ? 1 : 0, &quot;Signal&quot;)\" aria-label=\"Script or formula\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\">//@version=5\nindicator(\"x\")\nplot(ta.cum(volume))</textarea><div class=\"_editor_18fb12\" data-testid=\"pine-editor\" data-dialect=\"pine\"><div class=\"cm-editor ͼ1 ͼ2 \"><div class=\"cm-announced\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"cm-scroller\"><div class=\"cm-gutters cm-gutters-before\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"min-height: 56px; position: sticky;\"><div class=\"cm-gutter cm-gutter-lint\"><div class=\"cm-gutterElement\" style=\"height: 20.363636363636363px; margin-top: 36.27272727272727px;\"><div class=\"cm-lint-marker cm-lint-marker-error\"></div></div></div></div><div style=\"tab-size: 4;\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocorrect=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" writingsuggestions=\"false\" translate=\"no\" contenteditable=\"true\" class=\"cm-content cm-lineWrapping\" role=\"textbox\" aria-multiline=\"true\" aria-label=\"Script or formula editor\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"pine\" aria-autocomplete=\"list\"><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_comment_18fb12\">//@version=5</span></div><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_keyword_18fb12\">indicator</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"_string_18fb12\">\"x\"</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">)</span></div><div class=\"cm-line\"><span class=\"_keyword_18fb12\">plot</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"cm-lintRange cm-lintRange-error\"><span class=\"_namespace_18fb12\">ta</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">.</span><span class=\"_name_18fb12\">cum</span></span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">(</span><span class=\"_series_18fb12\">volume</span><span class=\"_punctuation_18fb12\">))</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"_report_5ff86c\"><p class=\"_meta_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-meta\" data-dialect=\"pine\">Read as Pine script v5 · indicator() · “x”</p><p class=\"_meta_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"import-outcome\" data-outcome=\"unsupported\" role=\"status\"><b>Not supported</b></p><div class=\"_notice_f5ec45\" role=\"status\" data-testid=\"import-gap-notice\" data-gaps=\"1\"><span>1 part of this script isn’t supported yet, so the chart may differ from TradingView: ta.cum.</span></div><div class=\"_refusal_5ff86c\" role=\"alert\" data-testid=\"pine-refusal\" data-guard=\"pine:function\"><span class=\"_refusalHead_5ff86c\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"url(#uig2)\" stroke-width=\"1.85\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" style=\"color: rgb(230, 205, 138); filter: drop-shadow(0 0 1.6px rgba(201,168,76,0.32));\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"uig2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#a8823a\"></stop><stop offset=\"40%\" stop-color=\"#d4b25a\"></stop><stop offset=\"50%\" stop-color=\"#e8d18c\"></stop><stop offset=\"60%\" stop-color=\"#cba954\"></stop><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#8f6f2c\"></stop></linearGradient></defs><path d=\"M12 4l9 16H3z\"></path><path d=\"M12 10v4.2M12 17.4v.2\"></path></svg><span class=\"_refusalWhere_5ff86c\">Line 3, column 6</span></span><span class=\"_refusalText_5ff86c\">`ta.cum` is a running total from the first bar, and `cum` names no anchor — a translator that picked one would be inventing the single number the whole answer turns on, and the value would then change with how many bars the chart requested. This engine declares `cumFrom(source, anchor, window)`, which is the same running total with the starting instant STATED: give it a unix-second anchor and it translates. `sum(source, n)` is the other answer when a fixed rolling window is what you meant.</span><pre class=\"_excerpt_5ff86c\">plot(ta.cum(volume))\n     ^</pre></div><div class=\"_notesWrap_5ff86c\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"_notesToggle_5ff86c\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-testid=\"pine-notes-toggle\">Show 1 line a screen does not read</button></div><p class=\"_refLink_5ff86c\"><a href=\"/formulas/reference\">See every name you can write →</a><a href=\"/formulas/library\">Browse what other members published →</a></p><button type=\"button\" class=\"_useBtn_5ff86c\" data-testid=\"pine-use\" disabled=\"\">Use this formula</button></div></section>",
